- review/ two-stage CI security scripts and workflow templates (Session 18) are
  adapted from TauCetiProject/TauCeti
  (https://github.com/TauCetiProject/TauCeti) at commit
  92c79e5e0a618f8c5c2b9909be1ce50f6891dde7 (2026-07-23), licensed Apache-2.0. That
  repo declares no copyright holder and ships no NOTICE (so there is no Apache §4(d)
  content to propagate); the adapted files carry an in-file `Adapted from …@92c79e5`
  header and a §4(b) change note. Files:
    * review/scope_guard.sh ← .github/workflows/pr-build.yml (the "Scope guard" step),
      extracted as a standalone script and hardened (any-depth allowlist, >3000-file
      cap, explicit gh-error/SIGPIPE fail-close).
    * review/authorize.sh ← .github/workflows/review.yml (the authorize step),
      extracted as a standalone script and hardened (distinct exit codes for
      API-error vs deny, 404-non-collaborator handling, env-not-inline injection safety).
    * review/pr-build.yml ← .github/workflows/pr-build.yml (generalised two-stage
      build template: pull_request_target overlay + scope guard + landrun + status handoff).
    * review/review.yml ← .github/workflows/review.yml (generalised privileged-review
      template: workflow_run/issue_comment, authorize, secrets only after build-status pass).
    * review/scripts/sandbox-build.sh ← scripts/sandbox-build.sh (generalised confined
      build; project-specific audits left to the adopting repo).
    * review/scripts/sandbox-selftest.sh ← the inline landrun self-test in pr-build.yml
      (extracted + hardened: positive control, no unsatisfiable UDP-deny, fail-closed host).
    * review/scripts/landrun-wrap.sh ← the `landrun` invocation in the "Build (sandboxed)"
      step of .github/workflows/pr-build.yml (the mount/`--env` flag set and the
      TMPDIR-inside-the-writable-mount pattern), extracted as a reusable shell wrapper and
      changed: pass-through when sandboxing is disabled, explicit fail-closed when enabled
      but landrun is absent, and the flag decision delegated to scripts/sandbox_flag.sh.
      (Recorded in Session 18r: this file was previously undeclared. The upstream
      comparison was made directly against pr-build.yml at the pinned commit.)
  landrun (github.com/Zouuup/landrun, MIT) is used as a pinned + SHA256-verified binary,
  not vendored. The pinned version is recorded in review/pr-build.yml and review/review.yml
  (v0.1.14 + SHA256); MIT, Copyright (c) 2025 Armin ranjbar; upstream ships no NOTICE.
  review/scripts/sandbox_flag.sh is NOT part of the above: `LEANREPO_SANDBOX` is this
  repository's own concept with no upstream counterpart, so that file is original work
  even though it was factored out of landrun-wrap.sh (only the flag parser moved, none of
  the landrun invocation that makes that file a derivative).

- review/lean_tools.py's environment ALLOWLIST takes its *technique* — allowlist rather
  than denylist for the environment handed to a child that elaborates untrusted Lean —
  from leanprover/lean-eval (https://github.com/leanprover/lean-eval), licensed
  Apache-2.0 (verified 2026-08-04 at commit
  6af65bb1abb997a3cfabf3236e43ab5085a51dac; that repo ships no NOTICE, so there is no
  Apache §4(d) content to propagate). **Concept-only reuse:** no lean-eval file is
  copied, adapted, or distributed here, and the two allowlists are not the same — theirs
  is minimal ({PATH, HOME, LEAN_ABORT_ON_PANIC}, tolerating LEAN_PATH and
  LD_LIBRARY_PATH), while ours is substantially broader (toolchain, locale, TLS trust
  roots, proxy, poppler/fontconfig) and adds a secret-name regex, a CA-path exemption,
  and a never-forward hard floor. Recorded because the in-code comment credits the idea;
  no §4 obligation arises from an unimplemented idea. The commit above is the tip at the
  time of verification, NOT a claim about which revision was originally consulted.

